.TH SLRXFM-GUI 1 "October 2026" "slrxfm 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slrxfm-gui \- Smech Labs Remastered Xandros File Manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slrxfm-gui
.RI [ directory ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slrxfm-gui
is a clean-room, from-scratch reimplementation of the behavior of
.BR XandrosFileManager ,
the proprietary file manager shipped with Xandros Desktop 1.0 (2002),
part of a broader historical-preservation and software-recreation
project for that distribution. No original Xandros code, decompiled
or otherwise, is present in this program; see
.I /usr/share/doc/slrxfm/CLEAN_ROOM.md
for the full clean-room methodology and evidence trail.
.PP
It presents a folder tree alongside a file-detail listing, and
supports the usual file-manager operations: copy, cut, paste, delete,
and rename; move-to-trash, restore, and empty-trash; symlink creation;
and browsing of local, SMB, FTP, and WebDAV locations through one
unified interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I directory
Optional. The directory to open on startup. Defaults to the user's
home directory.
.PP
Standard Qt options (e.g.
.B \-platform
and
.BR \-style )
are also accepted; see the upstream Qt documentation for the full
list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/slrxfm/trash
Default trash directory used by the move-to-trash/restore/empty-trash
operations.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation and the clean-room methodology are installed under
.IR /usr/share/doc/slrxfm/ .
Upstream project:
.UR https://github.com/Smech-Labs/slrxfm
.UE
.SH AUTHOR
Smech Labs <smechlabs@noreply.smech.dev>
